  "question": {
    "text": "The resistance of a wire is $R$. It is bent at the middle by $180^{\\circ}$ and both the ends are twisted together to make a shorter wire. The resistance of the new wire is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HGFfI",
      "text": "\n$2 R$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LVJKX",
      "text": "\n$R / 2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "062FA",
      "text": "\n$R / 4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Hmijk",
      "text": "\n$R / 8$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Resistance of wire $(R)=\\rho \\frac{l}{A}$ If wire is bent in the middle then\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& l^{\\prime}=\\frac{l}{2}, A^{\\prime}=2 \\mathrm{~A} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\text { New resistance, } \\mathrm{R}^{\\prime}=\\rho \\frac{l^{\\prime}}{\\mathrm{A}^{\\prime}} \\\\\n& =\\frac{\\rho \\frac{l}{2}}{2 A}=\\frac{\\rho l}{4 A}=\\frac{R}{4} \\text {. } \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
